# Install and test a snap on a Core device
End-to-end validation of a new snap revision on real hardware.

## 1. Build the snap
Run snapcraft in your snap's source directory:

  snapcraft

Verify the .snap file was produced and note its filename.

## 2. Set up device access
Confirm SSH access to the device. If using a VM, start it first:

  idiot vm run <image.img>

Then connect: idiot vm ssh  (or: ssh <user>@<device-ip>)

## 3. Copy the snap to the device
Use scp or idiot vm scp to transfer the file:

  idiot vm scp <snap-file> remote:~/

## 4. Install the snap
On the device, install from the local file:

  sudo snap install --dangerous ~/<snap-file>

Omit --dangerous if the snap is signed.

## 5. Verify snap status
  snap list <snap-name>
  snap info <snap-name>

Check the revision matches what you built.

## 6. Check interface connections
  snap connections <snap-name>

Verify all required plugs are connected. Connect any that aren't:

  sudo snap connect <snap-name>:<plug> <target-snap>:<slot>

## 7. Review snap logs
  snap logs <snap-name> -n 100

Look for startup errors or unexpected output.

## 8. Run functional tests
Exercise the snap's core functionality per your test plan.
Check that services started correctly:

  snap services <snap-name>

## 9. Review snap changes
  sudo snap changes

Confirm no changes are in Error or Doing state.
Use idiot inspect image to inspect an offline image if needed.
